TI  - Cerebral blood flow changes in patients with conversion disorder
T2  - PSYCHIATRY RESEARCH-NEUROIMAGING
M3  - Article
AB  - We evaluated regional cerebral blood how in five patients with conversion disorder (three females, two males, mean age +/- S.D.: 29.8 +/- 9.5 years) with astasia-abasia. The patients underwent single photon emission computed tomography after the injection of 555 MBq of [Tc-99m]hexamethylpropyleneamine oxime. Uptake ratios between areas of decreased perfusion and normal brain regions were considered significantly decreased when there was a change greater than or equal to 10%. Four of the five patients had left temporal and one patient had left parietal perfusion decreases. Uptake ratios ranged from 0.72 to 0.88 (mean +/- S.D.: 0.81 +/- 0.08). Our findings suggest that alterations in regional brain perfusion may accompany conversion symptoms. Functional imaging may therefore offer a means of elucidating the neural correlates of conversion disorder. (C) 1998 Elsevier Science Ireland Ltd. All rights reserved.
