TI  - Psychogenic Tremor:  Functional Magnetic Resonance Study on Emotional Processing
M3  - Awarded Grant
AB  - Psychogenic tremor belongs to a group of conditions caused by psychological stress factors, known as psychogenic movement disorders. This study seeks to understand what changes occur in the activity of the brain of people with psychogenic tremor, which may explain how their tremor is different from other forms of tremor and from people without tremor. Also this study will appraise how cognitive behavioral therapy, a form of psychological therapy, may help the tremor and overall psychological make up of people with psychogenic tremor.
