AB  - This meeting, which focuses on neurosurgery and psychiatry, contains approximately 17 oral abstracts and 21 lists poster presentations in English. Topics include differential diagnosis in relation to Huntington's disease, development of disease modifying therapies in Huntington's disease, disruption of brain connectivity in schizophrenia, initial treatment retention to habit reversal training in tourette syndrome, and acetylcholinesterase inhibitors for schizophrenia. Other topics are non epileptic seizures and todd's paresis-case series and literature review, frontal white matter connections and cognitive change in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis-a DTI-tractography study, and illness perceptions of neurologists and psychiatrists in relation to epilepsy and non-epileptic attack disorder (NESD).
