TI  - Psychogenic nonepileptic seizures in a patient with non-communicating hydrocephalus
T2  - RAWAL MEDICAL JOURNAL
M3  - Article
AB  - We report a 24-year-old female, who had non-communicating hydrocephalus, presenting with repeated paroxysmal-altered behaviors that resembled epileptic seizures. Positive responses to an antiepileptic drug and progressive changes in motor manifestations with abnormality on her brain MRI exacerbated the diagnosis of her symptoms. Repeated observation and examinations, including video-EEG monitoring, revealed that her symptoms resulted not from epileptic seizures but rather from psychogenic nonepileptic seizures.
